  "quality": "detailed",
  "visualBrief": "Grey tiled halls, red timber frames, green lattice screens and pale stone thresholds surround the Water Training School courts. A sheltered southern gallery and separate waterside structures sit above the native pond. The Water Village court to the north has grey tiles, broad dark timber and glass doors, and low stone sills. The south range has a recessed veranda with irregular stone under the windows and a narrow central stair. A short walk and stone landing join the south-range approach to the veranda.",
