    "notes": "Fourteen occupied PMTiles footprints establish the Water Training School courts, inland gallery, waterfront pavilions and the three northern ranges in the Water Village court. The native shoreline, ponds and public paths are retained. Individual room names, heights and courtyard paving are approximate. The small entry gate and fence lack a mapped footprint. The south range has a recessed timber-and-glass front, an open veranda, irregular stone infill and a narrow central step. Its approach strip in the overhead view supports the south-facing trial. The tea-house attribution and the position of its separate gate remain provisional."
